SUMMARY:Family Constellations: Subconscious Patterns in our Everyday Relati
 onships
DESCRIPTION:Family Constellations is a therapeutic approach and practice th
 at recognizes how our family's emotional history lives within us\, often u
 nconsciously shaping our experiences\, behaviors\, and struggles. Develope
 d by Psychotherapist\, Bert Hellinger\, this method acknowledges that heal
 ing often needs to happen at both an individual and systemic level.While t
 raditional talk therapy primarily focuses on individual healing\, Family C
 onstellations expands our perspective to include the entire family system.
 &nbsp\;When we think of the Soul a lot comes to mind — and most of it is
  often confusing because the one fact everyone agrees on is that it is som
 ething we cannot see nor fully grasp. What is the Soul? Does it even exist
 ? How can we understand it?Mystics like Theresa of Avila\, scholars\, arti
 sts\, philosophers\, scientists\, and even different religions have long t
 ried to make sense of the Soul\, find ways to capture it\, and/or question
  its existence.In this Olio we'll explore the Soul through the lens of Fam
 ily Constellations: an interior landscape where much of our past and that 
 of our ancestors is stored. We look at the Soul as a map that helps us nav
 igate through ancestral entanglements and blocked movements within us whic
 h don’t allow us to move forward in our everyday lives.&nbsp\;Listening 
 to\, uncovering\, and learning from these Soul movements form the core pra
 ctice of Family &amp\; Systemic Constellation work.Through interactive lec
 ture and a brief guided meditation\, we will get invited to explore our ow
 n Soul movements to help us better understand ourselves\, our loved ones\,
  our family\, and the people around us. We will then get the chance to exp
 erience a constellation in action with anyone who would like to participat
 e. No one will be asked to who is not willing and no prior experience is n
 eeded.Our teacher for the evening: Luisa Muhr is a New York–based interd
 isciplinary artist and Family &amp\; Systemic Constellations practitioner\
 , originally from Vienna\, Austria\, with Hungarian and Anatolian-Greek ro
 ots. She considers herself a “Field Worker” and was introduced to Fami
 ly Constellations in early childhood. Muhr later studied with her mentor D
 r. Peter Orban\, who grew out of the early Constellation work in Germany. 
 Alongside her healing arts practice\, Muhr is an experimental vocalist and
  interdisciplinary artist whose work spans voice\, sound\, movement\, impr
 ovisation\, installation\, performance art\, and experimental music theate
 r. The evening flow: 7:00pm- Doors open\, grab a drink and get settled&nbs
 p\;7:30pm - Olio Begins!8:30 - 8:45pm - Audience Q&amp\;A&nbsp\;9:00-10:00
 pm - Mingling at the Lighthouse&nbsp\;What Is an Olio?Think Olio is an ong
 oing experiment in lifelong learning. We are a community of open-minded pe
 ople who gather to exchange ideas with new friends and connect over art\, 
 literature\, and philosophy.Check out our full calendarOur $30 membership 
 gives you two events for the price of one!&nbsp\;An Olio is what we call t
 he social learning events we’ve been organizing since 2015. A blend betw
 een a lecture and a house party\, Olios are led by a teacher who loves sha
 ring their passions and the room is filled with curious\, open-minded New 
 Yorkers.&nbsp\;Our goal is to spark new perspectives\, ignite curiosity\, 
 and enjoy ourselves socially offering an alternative to typical nightlife 
 options.Disclaimer: By purchasing a ticket\, you agree to have your photo/
 video used for social media/marketing materials. If you prefer to not have
  your photo taken\, feel free to send us a note.Photo by Zhi-Da Zhong\n\nT
 ickets & info: https://www.viewcy.com/event/family_constellations
URL:https://www.viewcy.com/event/family_constellations
END:VEVENT
