SUMMARY:One Year Anniversary: Olio Homecoming Dance 2026
DESCRIPTION:Our little venue is officially one year old!!&nbsp\;And we’ve
  recently become obsessed with the idea of Olio running more like a public
  school (all the parts we love at least). Dances\, yearbooks\, field trips
 \, picture day\, etc… so for our one-year anniversary party we’ve deci
 ded to throw a Homecoming Dance.&nbsp\;Hang with your fellow Olio members\
 , dance\, smoke a cheeky cig on the roof during a crisp fall night\, come 
 back and dance and tune in for our highlight reel from the first year and 
 what's going to be even better in year two.&nbsp\;Punchbowl!&nbsp\;Slow Da
 nces!&nbsp\;What to expect:8pm: Hang in the space and vote on the club ide
 as.9:00pm-9:30pm: Highlight reel from the last year and announcement of cl
 ub winners!  10:00pm - 1am: Dance Party + DJ set playing our favorite home
 coming tunes (probably early 2000's bangers) Along the Olio School lines\,
  we’re excited to launch extracurricular clubs! If you’ve had ideas ab
 out ways you want to gather with your friends/bring new people into your l
 ife through your passions but maybe have no idea where to host or need a l
 ittle help spreading the word\, we’re now taking submissions for monthly
  club ideas by members\, for members.&nbsp\;Pitch us one\, about anything 
 you'd love to gather people around. We'll pick 3 clubs to meet once a mont
 h at the Lighthouse for 3 months\, and each club leader gets a stipend per
  session.Dress classy because the winners will be announced during the Hom
 ecoming Dance.Pitch your club here. Submissions close Monday\, Nov 9.Ticke
 ts:To attend sign up for our monthly membership which gives you two credit
 s to use towards our events each month.&nbsp\;You must be 21 or older to a
 ttend.What is Think Olio?Think Olio is an ongoing experiment in lifelong l
 earning. We are a community of open-minded people who gather to exchange i
 deas with new friends and connect over art\, literature\, and philosophy.A
 n Olio is what we call the social learning events we’ve been organizing 
 since 2015. A blend between a lecture and a house party\, Olios are led by
  a teacher who loves sharing their passions and the room is filled with cu
 rious\, open-minded New Yorkers.&nbsp\;A year into creating a venue\, one 
 of our favorite feelings has been the moments where we’ve stepped outsid
 e of time. We’ve created a space where conversations don’t feel rushed
 \, people are greeted with hugs\, and as a community\, we spontaneously co
 me up with new ideas (like the dial-up-disco house party) and bring them t
 o life.Our goal is to spark new perspectives\, ignite curiosity\, and enjo
 y ourselves socially\, an alternative to typical nightlife options.Check o
 ut our full calendarDisclaimer: By purchasing a ticket\, you agree to have
  your photo/video used for social media/marketing materials. If you prefer
  to not have your photo taken\, feel free to send us a note.\n\nTickets & 
 info: https://www.viewcy.com/event/homecoming-olio
URL:https://www.viewcy.com/event/homecoming-olio
END:VEVENT
