SUMMARY:Waking Up Our Dreams: Deciphering the Speech of the Soul
DESCRIPTION:Waking Up Our Dreams: What are dreams all about? and How can we
  engage with them?Dreaming is one of the most mysterious parts of being hu
 man. There are many theories about why we dream and many practices that ai
 m to help us understand our dreams. Are they just our brains processing wh
 at we've experienced? Are they prophetic visions offering glimpses of what
  lies ahead?Carl Jung's radical and profound studies of the unconscious ch
 anged our understanding of dreams in ways the culture is still digesting\,
  developing\, and passing on.In recent decades\, Jung's work has inspired 
 methods for working with dreams that have been embraced by psychoanalysts 
 and artists alike. Actors and writers in particular are increasingly turni
 ng to Dreamwork as a way to bypass the ego and draw their creative work fr
 om the unconscious\, a well of truth\, mystery\, symbolism\, and deep feel
 ing that exists within all of us.Ken Barnett comes to Olio to share some u
 nderstanding of dreams\, along with a few simple tools anyone can use to e
 ngage with their images and dynamics. We'll talk about the function of dre
 ams and try some simple\, creative exercises designed to draw our dreams c
 loser to us.As Jung said:"I must learn that the dregs of my thought\, my d
 reams\, are the speech of my soul. &nbsp\;I must carry them in my heart\, 
 and go back and forth over them in my mind\,&nbsp\;like the words of the p
 erson dearest to me. &nbsp\;Dreams are the guiding words of the soul. &nbs
 p\;Why should I henceforth not love my dreams and not make their riddling 
 images into objects of my daily consideration?”Our teacher for the eveni
 ngKen Barnett is an actor\, director\, acting coach\, and teacher of Dream
 work for Artists. He trained extensively with his mentor\, Kim Gillingham\
 , in Los Angeles\, and continued his studies with the Jungian Psychoanalyt
 ic Association of New York\, the C.G. Jung Foundation\, and Pacifica Gradu
 ate Institute. For 15 years he has coached actors\, writers\, and artists 
 in New York and LA\, leading workshops at The Schott Acting Studio in Berl
 in\, The Actors Center Workshop Company\, New York Stage &amp\; Film\, and
  Space on Ryder Farm. As an actor\, he has worked on and off Broadway for 
 over thirty years\, with TV roles on Mad Men\, House of Cards\, Mozart in 
 the Jungle\, and High Maintenance. The evening flow: 7:00pm- Doors open\, 
 grab a drink and get settled&nbsp\;7:30pm - Olio Begins!8:30 - 8:45pm - Au
 dience Q&amp\;A&nbsp\;9:00-10:00pm - Mingling at the Lighthouse&nbsp\;What
  Is an Olio?Think Olio is an ongoing experiment in lifelong learning. We a
 re a community of open-minded people who gather to exchange ideas with new
  friends and connect over art\, literature\, and philosophy.Check out our 
 full calendarOur $30 membership gives you two events for the price of one!
 &nbsp\;An Olio is what we call the social learning events we’ve been org
 anizing since 2015. A blend between a lecture and a house party\, Olios ar
 e led by a teacher who loves sharing their passions and the room is filled
  with curious\, open-minded New Yorkers.&nbsp\;Our goal is to spark new pe
 rspectives\, ignite curiosity\, and enjoy ourselves socially offering an a
 lternative to typical nightlife options.Disclaimer: By purchasing a ticket
 \, you agree to have your photo/video used for social media/marketing mate
 rials. If you prefer to not have your photo taken\, feel free to send us a
  note.Photo by Zhi-Da Zhong\n\nTickets & info: https://www.viewcy.com/even
 t/waking_up_our_dreams
URL:https://www.viewcy.com/event/waking_up_our_dreams
END:VEVENT
